ets are utilized to aid in the restoration of digestive function after a period of fasting, ensuring that patients can gradually reintroduce food in a manner that is safe and conducive to their healing process.", "DIETAS ESPECIALES:Special diets are non-coded diets tailored to individual patient needs.", "NUTRIENT DISTRIBUTION:Nutrient distribution in hospital diets typically consists of 50-55% carbohydrates, 30-35% lipids, and 10-20% proteins.", "DIETARY RESTRICTIONS:Dietary restrictions are essential for managing the health of patients with adrenoleucodistrofia, primarily aimed at limiting the intake of very long-chain fatty acids. In addition to this specific restriction, dietary guidelines for these patients may also encompass a variety of other limitations, including gluten-free, low-purine, and vegetarian options. These comprehensive dietary restrictions are designed to support the overall well-being and nutritional needs of individuals affected by this condition.", "ODONTOLOGICAL/FÁCIL MASTICACIÓN:Odontological/easy chewing diets are tailored for patients with chewing or swallowing difficulties.", "HIPERPROTEICA:HIPERPROTEICA refers to a high-protein diet specifically designed for patients who require an increased protein intake. This includes individuals suffering from conditions such as burns or those experiencing metabolic stress, where the body’s protein needs are elevated. The Hiperproteica diet is particularly beneficial for patients with burns or increased catabolism, as it helps support recovery and maintain muscle mass during periods of heightened protein demand.", "DIABÉTICA NIÑOS PEQUEÑOS:Diabetic diets for small children are designed for children under 6 years with diabetes.", "DIABÉTICA NIÑOS GRANDES:Diabetic diets for older children are tailored for children over 6 years with diabetes.", "CELÍACA:Celíaca diets are gluten-free diets for patients with gluten intolerance.", "POBRE EN COLESTEROL:Pobre en colesterol diets are low-cholesterol diets aimed at patients with dyslipidemia.", "LAXANTE:Laxante diets are designed for patients suffering from constipation.", "NO CARNE:No carne diets are for patients with meat intolerance.", "FÁCIL DIGESTIÓN:", "LUNES:Lunes is the Spanish word for Monday, representing the first day of the week in the diet plan.", "MARTES:Martes is the Spanish word for Tuesday, representing the second day of the week in the diet plan."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}